statement:
Call a password strong when all three rules hold:

- its length is between 6 and 20 characters, inclusive;
- it has a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter and a digit (at least one of each);
- no character occurs three or more times consecutively (`"xyyyz1A"` breaks this rule, `"xyyzy1A"` does not).

A single step either inserts one character anywhere, deletes one character, or changes one character into any other character. Return the fewest steps that turn `password` into a strong password, which is `0` when it is strong already.

validator:
function validate([password]) {
  if (typeof password !== 'string') return 'password must be a string.';
  if (password.length < 1 || password.length > 50) return 'password needs 1 to 50 characters.';
  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9.!]+$/.test(password)) return "Use only letters, digits, '.' and '!'.";
  return null;
}

